  "detail": "`protectedRequest` exempts GET and HEAD everywhere except `/api/admin*` and `/mcp`. Codex editors keep loopback network (no port deny), and an implementer can read its own run id from its worktree path or branch name. Measured against the running release on main: `GET /api/runs/<id>/artifacts/holdout-scenarios.json` returns 200 with the hidden scenarios. A temporary probe at this head, with `require_api_token = true`, got 200 and seeded content without credentials for `holdout-scenarios.json`, `verify-1.json` and run detail including the prompt. All three SSE routes (`/api/stream`, `/api/runs/:id/stream`, `/api/chat/:id/stream`) also returned 200. Run lists and detail, events, artifacts, chat and feed expose other runs' data as well, and holdouts are what keeps verification blind. The issue leaves only `GET /api/health` open. Fix: when enforcement is on, every route needs the token or a session, except `/api/health`, the sign-in pages and assets the sign-in page needs, the passkey sign-in endpoints, and the signature-verified `/webhooks/*`. Update the clients that read (setup's `/api/github/access`, `follow()`, MCP reads) and keep the loopback UI usable through sign-in (see the sign-in finding). Test: with enforcement on, a credential-free loopback GET of an artifact, run detail, events and each stream gets 401, and the same requests with the token or a session succeed."
