  "detail": "`/api/auth/logout-all` is token-exempt, and its handler (around line 251) revokes every session without first checking that the caller has one. A temporary probe sent an anonymous POST and got `200 {\"revoked\":1}`, and the owner fixture's cookie stopped working. Any process that can reach loopback, including a Codex editor, can sign the owner out repeatedly. Fix: revoking all sessions needs a valid session or the token. Anonymous `/api/auth/logout` may stay exempt, since it only clears the caller's own cookie. Test: an anonymous `logout-all` gets 401 and leaves the owner's session working, and an authenticated one still revokes."
