  "title": "Land checks resumed at startup can run before the token file is read-protected",
  "detail": "The token is created and registered as a private read path inside `startHttp`, but the daemon starts the land queue and integrations first (src/cli/main.ts:203, src/integrations/index.ts:47). A temporary startup probe saw `land.start()` before the token was registered. A confinement profile built at that point lacked the token's denyRead, and one built after token creation had it. A gate launched during that window keeps its earlier profile, so it can read the token once the file is written. Fix: create and protect the token before anything that can launch confined work (land queue, scheduler, resumed runs, integrations). Test: start the daemon with a queued land entry, and assert the first confined command's profile denies the token path."
 },
 {
